=== bonsai_fleet ring 4 8 6, v2 (02:05 2026-11-05) ===
  v1 of this log (fleet_ring_v1.log) kept: it is the run that showed 6 phantom mismatches
  and the impossible 56 GB/s batched rate. Both had one root cause - the ring cursor was a STAGE
  sequence while only every nb-th stage is a payload, and the fenced/batched timing trusted a fence
  without checking the queue tail. This run adds the fence-vs-queue-idle audit and the payload
  cross-check, and the pipeline now counts payloads. See gpu_fleet.h (1) block and cmd_ring.


== fleet ring rig: depth 4 x 8 MiB slots, 6 microbatch(es) ==
  card [0] Radeon RX 550X (DISCRETE_GPU) | compute family 0 | transfer-only family 2
  arena type 0  DEVICE_LOCAL   24.0 MiB  [shared-heap=no cached=no]  <- discrete branch: first type carrying DEVICE_LOCAL, exactly the predicate every existing runs/ log was produced with
  ring: 4 slot(s) x 8388608 B = 33554432 B, memory type 3 (host-visible, not on a unified heap)
  pipelined run below moves each 8388608 B slot D2H out of PROD and H2D into CONS, so the
  bytes cross the link twice per hop. NOT EXERCISABLE HERE: only one compute-capable device was opened, so the second card's H2D->compute overlap and the PCIe-to-PCIe path a two-card machine takes are untested, and the D2H->host->H2D round trip is what IS tested.

  pipelined run: 12 stage(s), 6 hop(s) in 18.783 ms
  per hop: wall 3130.5 us | host-visible waits: D2H fence 1.7 us, back-pressure 3.6 us total over 2 wait(s), command-buffer recycle 5927.2 us total over 8 wait(s)
  bytes across the ring: 50331648 B total, 8.00 MiB per hop; at the MEASURED 7.12 GB/s a 8388608 B slot is 1178.18 us of engine time per leg, so a hop is SYNC-dominated (MEASURED submit+fence round trip 99.4 us)
  back-pressure events: 2 at depth 4 (a depth-1 ring would take one wait per hop; D>1 is the mechanism, not a tuning knob)
  ring cursors: produced 6, consumed 6 (equal, as they must be after the drain)
  cursor cross-check: produced 6 vs hops 6 -> consistent
  D2H arrival: 12 word(s) read through the ring mapping over 4 written slot(s) (0 untouched), 0 mismatch(es) -> PASS - the DMA put into the slot exactly what the producer's dispatch wrote into its window, and the publish happened after the fence
  round trip slot1 -> CONS -> slot2: bytes intact (fence 1.0 / 0.8 us, + queue-idle 1198.9 / 1203.0 us; each leg is copy + one submit+fence round trip, MEASURED 99.4 us)
  fenced D2H audit: the fence alone reported 1.3 us per hop, the queue-idle tail after it added 1255.3 us (a tail near zero means the fence IS the completion signal here)
  fenced D2H  8 x 8388608 B on family 2: 1256.6 us per hop -> 6.68 GB/s wall = 93% of the MEASURED 7.15 GB/s ceiling, submit and fence included
  batched D2H 8 x 8388608 B in ONE submit: fence 0.7 us total, queue-idle tail 9413.9 us total -> 1176.8 us per copy, 7.13 GB/s end-to-end (MEASURED single-copy ceiling 7.15 GB/s; if the fence column alone exceeds it, the fence is not the completion signal and the SUM is the number to quote)
  device released. Whole command took 107 ms of GPU-touching time.
